ian control but this area is  heavily contested at the moment  and there isn't really any part of this  city  that hasn't been hit by  russian attacks  this was an airstrike  now nobody was killed incredibly and the  police are managing to still work  out of the rest of this building  but it's a scene of absolute devastation  everyone in this city is struggling in  the face of unrelenting savagery  as we visit the only working hospital  the sound of fighting gets closer  inside the medics do what they can  they're treating the war wounded and  routine emergencies people don't stop  getting sick because they're shooting  outside  all of the patients are treated in the  corridors away from the windows which  have been blown out by shells  this hospital has been attacked more  than 20 times  is recovering from shrapnel wounds but  she's defiant and has this message for  vladimir putin  and after we left we received these  images from medics  the hospital had been shelled again and  one of the patients was killed  it is another reminder of the brutal  nature of russia's war  where the innocent are all too often the  victims  alex rossi sky news eastern ukraine  potentially thousands of civilians and  troops remained trapped in a steel plant  in ukraine the azov style complex uh  well it's situated in the besieged city  of mario paul in the south of ukraine  and local officials say the plant is  once again  under russian  bombardment uh joining me now yuri  rosenkoff the ceo of met invest holding  which owns the as of style steel plant  in mario paul um yuri thank you so much  for taking the time to talk to us this  morning i really appreciate it and i i  just wonder if you can give us  any up-to-date information of what you  know to be the situation in and around  the steel plant you must suspect that  there are several thousand of your  employees still there  well unfortunately we don't even know  how many of our employees are still at  the plant uh  the situation ther